window.__READMES["Agentoscopy"]="<div id=\"readme\" class=\"md\" data-path=\"README.md\"><article class=\"markdown-body entry-content container-lg\" itemprop=\"text\"><div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h1 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Agentoscopy</h1><a id=\"user-content-agentoscopy\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Agentoscopy\" href=\"#agentoscopy\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">An evaluation harness for LLM agents, built to answer one question for a team changing an\nagent: did this change make it better or worse, and how sure can we be? Suites of tasks run\nas concurrent trials in Docker sandboxes, every model call goes through a budget-enforcing\ngateway, results land in SQLite, and runs can be compared statistically, from the CLI or\nin a local web UI. Trials are graded by commands, trajectory rules, a tamper check that\nvetoes reward hacking, and an LLM judge whose agreement with human reviewers is measured.\nRuns survive crashes and can be cancelled, and <code>agentoscopy ci</code> gates pull requests on\nregressions.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atikulmunna/Agentoscopy/HEAD/docs/compare.png\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atikulmunna/Agentoscopy/HEAD/docs/compare.png\" alt=\"The compare page: the example agent on Claude Haiku 5.5 against Claude Sonnet 5.5\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>The compare page for two real runs of the 20-task core suite, four trials per task: the\nexample Claude agent on Claude Sonnet 5.5 (the baseline, $0.93 for 80 trials) against the\nsame agent on Claude Haiku 5.5 ($0.12). Both models' fixes passed the hidden tests in all\n80 trials. The difference is the tamper check: Haiku also edited a task's protected test\nfile in 59 trials, adding tests of its own, and each of those is vetoed; Sonnet did so in\n2. <a href=\"#replay-and-fork\">Bisect</a> found where one of those Haiku trials went wrong.</em></p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">How it compares</h2><a id=\"user-content-how-it-compares\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How it compares\" href=\"#how-it-compares\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://inspect.aisi.org.uk/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Inspect</a> is a broad framework for writing and running\nevaluations. It ships over 200 ready-made evaluations, runs untrusted code in Docker,\nKubernetes, and other sandboxes, and can drive external agents such as Claude Code.\n<a href=\"https://github.com/SWE-bench/SWE-bench\">SWE-bench</a> is a benchmark: software issues\ncollected from GitHub, with a harness that applies the patch a system submits and runs the\nrepository's tests in Docker.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Agentoscopy is narrower. It is for a team iterating on one agent that needs to know whether\na change made it better or worse, and how far to trust the answer:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Paired comparison.</strong> Two runs are compared task by task. Each task is classified\n(regressed, improved, flaky, and so on) with an exact test, and the verdict comes from a\n95% confidence interval over tasks. A test checks that comparing a config with itself\ngives a false verdict only about 5% of the time.</li>\n<li><strong>CI gating.</strong> <code>agentoscopy ci</code> runs the suite on a pull request, compares it with the\nlatest run on main, comments the verdict, and fails the check on a regression.</li>\n<li><strong>Every model call through one gateway.</strong> The gateway enforces each trial's step, token,\nand cost budget and records every call, so a trial can be replayed from its recording,\nor forked at a step to see what another config would have done.</li>\n<li><strong>Grading that can be audited.</strong> A tamper check vetoes reward hacking, and LLM judge\nverdicts are sampled for human review, with each judge's agreement measured.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It is also smaller. The bundled tasks are a starter suite for exercising the harness, not a\nbenchmark, though <code>task import</code> turns fixes from your own repository's history into tasks;\nand agents are Python classes, or command-line agents such as Claude Code run inside the\nsandbox. To rank models,\nuse a benchmark such as SWE-bench; for a wide range of ready-made evaluations, Inspect; to\ngate changes to one agent, Agentoscopy.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Setup</h2><a id=\"user-content-setup\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Setup\" href=\"#setup\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Requires Python 3.11+, <a href=\"https://docs.astral.sh/uv/\" rel=\"nofollow\">uv</a>, and a running Docker daemon.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"uv sync\"><pre>uv sync</pre></div>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Workflow</h2><a id=\"user-content-workflow\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Workflow\" href=\"#workflow\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"uv run agentoscopy task validate --all                  # build images, run null/reference/isolation checks\nuv run agentoscopy task list                            # validation status of every task\nuv run agentoscopy task import ../myrepo &lt;commit&gt; --id fix-x  # a task from a fix in your repo's history\nuv run agentoscopy run --suite example --agent configs/scripted-fix.yaml --trials 3\nuv run agentoscopy report &lt;run_id&gt; --format md          # table, md, or json\nuv run agentoscopy compare &lt;baseline_run&gt; &lt;candidate_run&gt;\nuv run agentoscopy tradeoff &lt;run_id&gt; &lt;run_id&gt; ...        # pass rate against cost, and the frontier\nuv run agentoscopy run --resume &lt;run_id&gt;                # continue a run after a crash\nuv run agentoscopy replay &lt;trial_id&gt;                    # rerun a trial from its recorded model calls\nuv run agentoscopy fork &lt;trial_id&gt; --at-step 3          # the same up to step 3, then live\nuv run agentoscopy bisect &lt;trial_id&gt; --agent CONFIG     # the step where a failed trial went wrong\nuv run agentoscopy agent check configs/claude.yaml      # try an agent config before a real run\nuv run agentoscopy cancel &lt;run_id&gt;\nuv run agentoscopy gc --older-than 30d                  # old run outputs, orphaned sandboxes\nuv run agentoscopy serve                                # web UI; open the URL it prints\"><pre>uv run agentoscopy task validate --all                  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> build images, run null/reference/isolation checks</span>\nuv run agentoscopy task list                            <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> validation status of every task</span>\nuv run agentoscopy task import ../myrepo <span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;</span>commit<span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span> --id fix-x  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> a task from a fix in your repo's history</span>\nuv run agentoscopy run --suite example --agent configs/scripted-fix.yaml --trials 3\nuv run agentoscopy report <span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;</span>run_id<span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span> --format md          <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> table, md, or json</span>\nuv run agentoscopy compare <span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;</span>baseline_run<span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;</span>candidate_run<span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span>\nuv run agentoscopy tradeoff <span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;</span>run_id<span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;</span>run_id<span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span> ...        <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> pass rate against cost, and the frontier</span>\nuv run agentoscopy run --resume <span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;</span>run_id<span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span>                <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> continue a run after a crash</span>\nuv run agentoscopy replay <span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;</span>trial_id<span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span>                    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> rerun a trial from its recorded model calls</span>\nuv run agentoscopy fork <span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;</span>trial_id<span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span> --at-step 3          <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> the same up to step 3, then live</span>\nuv run agentoscopy bisect <span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;</span>trial_id<span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span> --agent CONFIG     <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> the step where a failed trial went wrong</span>\nuv run agentoscopy agent check configs/claude.yaml      <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> try an agent config before a real run</span>\nuv run agentoscopy cancel <span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;</span>run_id<span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span>\nuv run agentoscopy gc --older-than 30d                  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> old run outputs, orphaned sandboxes</span>\nuv run agentoscopy serve                                <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> web UI; open the URL it prints</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>agentoscopy run</code> takes <code>--suite NAME</code> or one or more <code>--task ID</code>, plus <code>--budget-usd</code> (run cost\nceiling, default 10), <code>--concurrency</code>, <code>--seed</code>, <code>--label KEY=VALUE</code>, <code>--judge-model</code>\n(default <code>claude-opus-5-5</code>), and <code>--review-rate</code> (the fraction of trials sampled for human\nreview, default 0.05). A task can only run once its current content has been validated.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To run only some of a suite's tasks, add <code>--tag</code>, <code>--category</code>, <code>--difficulty</code>, or\n<code>--failed-in RUN_ID</code> (the tasks that failed or hit an infra error in that run). Repeat an\noption for any of several values; different options must all match. A filtered run keeps\nthe suite's name but no suite version, so it never stands in for a full run of the suite\n(as a CI baseline, say), and it records the filter as a label.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>--top-up N</code> adds N more trials to every task whose trials both passed and failed, once the\nplanned trials are done, so extra trials go where the result is uncertain. A run that hit\nits budget is not topped up, and a resumed run still finishes its top-up.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The example task has an LLM judge grader, so validating and running it calls the judge\nmodel, which needs <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code>. To try everything offline, add <code>--judge-model mock</code>\nto both <code>task validate</code> and <code>run</code>. The mock judge answers at random, so expect the\ncalibration page to call it uncalibrated.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Exit codes: <code>0</code> success, <code>1</code> a task failed a validation check, <code>2</code> invalid input, <code>3</code>\nenvironment or harness failure, <code>130</code> the run was cancelled.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Crashes, resuming, and cancelling</h2><a id=\"user-content-crashes-resuming-and-cancelling\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Crashes, resuming, and cancelling\" href=\"#crashes-resuming-and-cancelling\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A trial in flight is held under a lease that its process renews every 10 seconds. If the\nprocess dies, the lease runs out after 30 seconds, and <code>agentoscopy run --resume &lt;run_id&gt;</code>\npicks the run up: it removes the containers and snapshots the dead attempts left behind,\ncounts what those attempts spent, and runs the trials again. A trial is finalised only by\nthe process that holds it, so nothing is lost or counted twice. Resuming needs the tasks\nto have the content the run started with.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>agentoscopy cancel &lt;run_id&gt;</code> (or the run page's Cancel button) cancels queued trials at\nonce. Trials that are setting up or running stop within a few seconds, with 30 seconds\nfor the agent to wind down; trials already being graded finish. Finished trials keep\ntheir results, and the run gets a partial summary. Ctrl-C in <code>agentoscopy run</code> is\nblunter: it cancels every unfinished trial at once, including any being graded.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>agentoscopy gc</code> deletes the trajectories and artifacts of runs that finished more than\n<code>--older-than</code> ago (results stay in the database; runs with trials waiting for review\nare kept), and removes sandboxes that no running trial holds. <code>--dry-run</code> only reports.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">CI gating</h2><a id=\"user-content-ci-gating\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: CI gating\" href=\"#ci-gating\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>agentoscopy ci --suite S --agent C --baseline main</code> runs the suite, compares it with the\nnewest completed run of the same suite version labelled <code>branch=main</code> (from the last 7\ndays, <code>--max-baseline-age</code>), and reports the verdict. With no such run it runs one first\nwith <code>--baseline-agent</code>. <code>--github</code> posts the comparison as a pull request comment and\nupdates that same comment on later pushes; inside GitHub Actions it needs only\n<code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code>. <code>--override</code> (the workflow sets it for the <code>eval-override</code> label) reports a\nregression without failing. Exit codes: <code>0</code> no regression, <code>1</code> regression, <code>2</code> harness\nerror, <code>3</code> the candidate run hit its budget.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>.github/workflows/eval.yml</code> wires this up: pull requests are evaluated against the\nbaseline that pushes to <code>main</code> keep fresh in the Actions cache, and pull requests from\nforks never run with provider credentials.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Comparing runs</h2><a id=\"user-content-comparing-runs\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Comparing runs\" href=\"#comparing-runs\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>agentoscopy compare</code> lines up the tasks both runs scored at the same version. Each task is\nclassified as regressed, improved, changed, flaky, stable pass, or stable fail; regressed\nand improved need a one-sided Fisher's exact test at p &lt; 0.05, which takes at least 4\ntrials per run (6 for tasks marked <code>critical</code>, which get those automatically). The\nverdict is <code>REGRESSION</code> when the 95% CI of the mean per-task change is below zero or a\ncritical task regressed, <code>IMPROVEMENT</code> when it is above zero, and <code>NO_SIGNIFICANT_CHANGE</code>\notherwise. The CI is a Student t interval over tasks: comparing a config with itself gives\na different verdict about 5% of the time, which a test checks. Every critical task is\nanother chance of a false alarm, so when a suite has several, a critical regression must\nsurvive a Holm correction across them; otherwise it is reported as a warning. With five\ncritical tasks, false verdicts stay near 6% instead of rising to about 14%, which a test\nalso checks. The output also shows cost, token, step, and duration\ndeltas, deltas by task category and tag, and a field-level diff of the two agent configs.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Cost against quality</h2><a id=\"user-content-cost-against-quality\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Cost against quality\" href=\"#cost-against-quality\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>agentoscopy tradeoff &lt;run_id&gt; &lt;run_id&gt; ...</code> weighs pass rate against cost across 2 to 20\nruns, and the web UI draws it when two or more runs are selected. It uses the tasks every\nrun scored at the same version, so a run over easier tasks cannot look better than it is.\nFor each run it gives the mean pass rate over those tasks, with the same 95% t interval\ncomparisons use, and the mean agent cost per scored trial; judge spend is left out, as it\nis from budgets. A run is on the frontier when no other run passes at least as often for no\nmore cost. The chart joins the frontier with a step line: the best pass rate each budget\nbuys. The frontier compares point estimates, so where intervals overlap, the order may not\nhold. <code>--format</code> takes <code>table</code>, <code>md</code>, or <code>json</code>, and the API is <code>GET /tradeoff?runs=A,B,C</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atikulmunna/Agentoscopy/HEAD/docs/tradeoff.png\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atikulmunna/Agentoscopy/HEAD/docs/tradeoff.png\" alt=\"The cost and quality page for three agent configs on the core suite\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Three real runs of the core suite, four trials per task. The example agent on Claude Haiku\n5.5 passes 26.3% of tasks at $0.0015 per trial, Claude Code on the same model 72.5% at\n$0.0020, and the example agent on Claude Sonnet 5.5 97.5% at $0.0116. None beats another on\nboth, so all three are on the frontier. Each of Claude Code's 22 failures was a tamper veto\nfor editing a protected test file, 20 of them on the tasks that ask for new code; its fixes\npassed the hidden tests in all 22.</em></p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Grading</h2><a id=\"user-content-grading\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Grading\" href=\"#grading\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Each trial is graded in a fresh sandbox cloned from the agent's final state, with caches\n(<code>__pycache__</code>, <code>.pytest_cache</code>) deleted first. A trial passes when every <code>required</code>\ngrader passes; its score is the weighted mean of all graders.</p>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Passes when</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>command</code></td>\n<td>its shell command exits 0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>forbidden_command</code></td>\n<td>no command the agent ran matches any of <code>patterns</code> (regexes)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>must_read_before_edit</code></td>\n<td>every existing file the agent wrote was read first</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>max_tool_errors</code></td>\n<td>at most <code>max</code> tool calls failed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>max_steps</code></td>\n<td>the agent made at most <code>max</code> model calls</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>tamper_check</code></td>\n<td>nothing changed outside <code>allowed_paths</code> (default: the workdir and <code>/tmp</code>) or inside <code>protected_paths</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>llm_judge</code></td>\n<td>the pinned judge model says the work meets <code>rubric</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The tamper check reads the whole-container filesystem diff, so it catches tampering\nhowever it was done. A failed tamper check is a veto: the trial fails with score 0 and\nthe failure tag <code>reward_hacking</code>, whatever the other graders said. Changes made by the\ntask's <code>setup</code> commands are recorded as a baseline and never count against the agent.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The judge sees the task, the rubric, and the agent's final message, changed files, and\nactions. Everything the agent produced is passed inside <code>&lt;agent_data&gt;</code> tags that the\njudge is told to treat as evidence, never as instructions. The judge answers with\nstructured output, its calls go through the gateway on their own budget (<code>max_cost_usd</code>,\ndefault $0.25 per trial), and judge spend is reported apart from agent spend. A judge\nthat fails, or returns unusable output 3 times, makes the trial an infra error, never a\nfailure of the agent. During validation each judge votes 3 times and the majority\ncounts; a task whose required graders are all judges is flagged <code>SOFT_GRADER_ONLY</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Human review and judge calibration</h2><a id=\"user-content-human-review-and-judge-calibration\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Human review and judge calibration\" href=\"#human-review-and-judge-calibration\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Runs add trials to a review queue: a random sample (<code>--review-rate</code>), every judge\nverdict with confidence below 0.7, and anything added by hand from a trial page. The\nqueue shows unsure judge verdicts first, then random samples, then hand-added items.\nFor a judge item the reviewer answers the rubric's question; other items are trial\naudits. The judge's verdict stays hidden until the review is submitted. Keys: <code>p</code> pass,\n<code>f</code> fail, <code>s</code> skip, <code>n</code> next. A reviewer can also override the trial's outcome; the\noriginal outcome is kept and the run summary is recomputed.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The calibration report gives, per task, judge grader, and judge model, the agreement\nrate, Cohen's kappa, the confusion matrix, and every disagreement. Agreement and kappa\nuse only randomly sampled reviews, since low-confidence and hand-added items are hard\ncases by design. A judge with kappa below 0.6 over at least 30 random reviews is\nflagged uncalibrated, and every run that uses it shows a warning.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Failed trials can be tagged from their page, with a tag from a short list (wrong fix,\nincomplete, misread task, and so on) or any other word. The run dashboard and\n<code>agentoscopy report</code> count the tags. Reviewers can remove the tags they added; the\n<code>reward_hacking</code> tag the tamper check adds stays. The API is <code>GET /failure-tags</code>,\n<code>POST /trials/{trial_id}/tags</code> with <code>tag</code> and an optional <code>note</code>, and\n<code>DELETE /trials/{trial_id}/tags/{tag}</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Web UI</h2><a id=\"user-content-web-ui\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Web UI\" href=\"#web-ui\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>agentoscopy serve</code> serves a UI on <code>127.0.0.1:8321</code>: the runs list (select two runs to\ncompare them, or two or more to weigh cost against quality), a run dashboard with one well\nper trial, trial pages with the event timeline, graders, and filesystem diff, the\ncomparison, side-by-side trajectories, the cost and quality chart, the review queue, and\njudge calibration. Every API call needs the token in the printed URL,\nand requests for other host names are refused. Runs started from the CLI appear live.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Runs can be started and cancelled over HTTP. <code>POST /runs</code> takes JSON with <code>agent</code> (the name\nof a config in <code>--configs-dir</code>, default <code>configs/</code>), either <code>suite</code> or <code>tasks</code>, and\noptionally <code>trials</code>, <code>budget_usd</code>, <code>concurrency</code>, <code>seed</code>, <code>labels</code>, <code>judge_model</code>, and\n<code>review_rate</code>; the run executes in the server process. <code>DELETE /runs/{run_id}</code> cancels\none. <code>GET /metrics</code> serves Prometheus metrics for every run in the database: queue depth,\ntrials in flight, outcomes, infra errors, trial durations, gateway latency, and spend.\nSet <code>AGENTOSCOPY_API_TOKEN</code> to give the server a fixed token, for example for a scraper.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Review endpoints: <code>GET /review/queue?limit=N</code>; <code>POST /review/queue</code> with <code>trial_id</code> and an\noptional <code>grader_name</code>, to add an item by hand; <code>POST /review/{review_id}</code> with <code>passed</code>\nand optional <code>score</code>, <code>note</code>, <code>reviewer</code>, and <code>override</code>, which answers with the judge's\nverdict; and <code>GET /calibration</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Agents</h2><a id=\"user-content-agents\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Agents\" href=\"#agents\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Agents are Python classes named by <code>entrypoint</code> in a config file under <code>configs/</code>. They\nreceive a recording sandbox handle and a per-trial gateway endpoint; use it as the\nAnthropic SDK's <code>base_url</code> and <code>api_key</code>.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code>scripted-fix</code>, <code>scripted-broken</code>, <code>scripted-malicious</code>: scripted test agents. They call\nthe <code>mock</code> model, which is seeded and costs nothing real.</li>\n<li><code>scripted-tamper-tests</code>, <code>scripted-tamper-conftest</code>: apply the correct fix but also\nrewrite a test or add a <code>conftest.py</code>; the tamper check must veto both.</li>\n<li><code>scripted-judge-injection</code>: fixes the bug, also rewrites an unrelated file, and tells\nthe judge to pass it. A real judge should still fail <code>minimal_change</code>.</li>\n<li><code>claude</code>: an example Claude agent (tool-use loop with <code>bash</code> and <code>write_file</code>). It needs\n<code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code>. The key is handed to a separate credential-proxy process and removed\nfrom the <code>agentoscopy</code> process before any agent code is imported.</li>\n<li><code>claude-sonnet</code>, <code>claude-haiku</code>: the same agent at medium effort on Claude Sonnet 5.5 and\nClaude Haiku 5.5, the two configs in the screenshot above.</li>\n<li><code>claude-code-haiku</code>: Claude Code itself, run inside the sandbox on Claude Haiku 5.5 (see\nbelow).</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h3 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Command-line agents</h3><a id=\"user-content-command-line-agents\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Command-line agents\" href=\"#command-line-agents\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>agentoscopy.adapters.command:CommandAgent</code> runs any command-line agent inside the sandbox.\nIts config gives <code>install</code> steps, which are built on top of the task image once per task\nimage; the <code>command</code>, where <code>{instructions}</code> becomes the task's instructions; and extra\n<code>env</code>. The command runs in the workdir with <code>ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL</code> set to a relay on the\nsandbox's own loopback address. The relay hands each request to the harness over the same\n<code>docker exec</code> channel the harness already uses, and the harness sends it to the trial's\ngateway with the trial's token. So the sandbox keeps no network at all, the agent never\nholds a credential, and the gateway enforces the trial's budget as for any other agent.\nThe task image needs <code>python3</code>, which runs the relay.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Exit code 0 ends the trial as <code>agent_done</code>, another code as an agent error, and running past\nthe task's timeout as <code>timeout</code>. Every model call is recorded; the agent's own tool calls\nhappen inside its process, so the trajectory shows them only as the one command and its\noutput, and trajectory graders have less to go on.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>configs/claude-code-haiku.yaml</code> installs Node 22 and Claude Code 2.1.310 and points every\nmodel Claude Code picks at <code>claude-haiku-5-5</code>. It passes <code>agentoscopy agent check</code>, and on\nthree core tasks the example Haiku agent always failed by editing protected tests, it passed\ntwo of them in both trials (4 of 6 trials, $0.013 in all).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>agentoscopy agent check &lt;config&gt;</code> runs a config once on a built-in smoke task (reverse a\nfile's contents). It passes when the agent called a model through the gateway, acted in\nthe sandbox or reported a message, and finished on its own. It fails with <code>GATEWAY_BYPASS</code>\nwhen the agent ignored the endpoint it was given, <code>NO_AGENT_EVENTS</code>, or\n<code>AGENT_DID_NOT_FINISH</code>. Whether the agent solved the smoke task is reported but does not\ndecide the check.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Once a trial's step, token, or cost budget is spent, the gateway rejects further calls with\nHTTP 400 and error type <code>budget_exceeded_error</code> (<code>agentoscopy.adapters.base.BUDGET_EXCEEDED_ERROR</code>).</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Tasks</h2><a id=\"user-content-tasks\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Tasks\" href=\"#tasks\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A task lives in <code>tasks/&lt;id&gt;/</code>:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code>task.yaml</code>: instructions, environment, budget, graders, and optional <code>category</code>,\n<code>difficulty</code>, <code>tags</code>, and <code>critical</code></li>\n<li><code>fixtures/</code>: copied into the workdir when the task image is built</li>\n<li><code>hidden/</code>: grader-only files, mounted read-only at <code>/hidden</code> during grading only</li>\n<li><code>reference/</code>: optional reference solution; its files overlay the workdir during validation</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Suites live in <code>suites/&lt;name&gt;.yaml</code> as a name and a list of task ids, a list of <code>tags</code>, or\nboth: a suite with tags also takes every task that carries one of them, after the listed\nones. <code>core</code> is a starter suite for trying the harness and comparing agents, not a\nbenchmark: twenty small Python tasks (thirteen bug fixes, six small features, and the\nexample task) of mixed difficulty, each with visible tests, hidden tests, a reference\nsolution, and the tamper check. <code>example</code> holds just the example task, the only one with an\nLLM judge. The run database, trajectories, and artifacts are written under <code>.agentoscopy/</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h3 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Tasks from your own repository</h3><a id=\"user-content-tasks-from-your-own-repository\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Tasks from your own repository\" href=\"#tasks-from-your-own-repository\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>agentoscopy task import &lt;repo&gt; &lt;commit&gt; --id ID</code> turns a commit that fixed a bug in a local\ngit repository into a task, so agents are measured on your code's real bugs:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>the commit before the fix is the starting code;</li>\n<li>the test files the fix added or changed are the hidden tests, at their fixed versions.\nTheir old versions are held back from the starting code, since they assert the bug;</li>\n<li>the other files the fix changed are the reference solution;</li>\n<li>the commit message is the instructions, unless <code>--instructions</code> says otherwise.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Then <code>agentoscopy task validate ID</code> checks that the hidden tests fail before the fix and pass\nwith it, as for any task. Tests run with <code>unittest</code> by default; <code>--runner pytest</code> installs\npytest in the image. <code>--build COMMAND</code> runs while the image is built, after the code is\ncopied in, for dependencies (<code>--build \"pip install -r requirements.txt\"</code>), and\n<code>--base-image</code> replaces the default Python 3.12 image (pin it by digest). Tag imports with\n<code>--tag myrepo</code> and a suite with <code>tags: [myrepo]</code> collects them all.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The repository is only read through git; nothing is fetched. A commit that changes no\ntests, changes only tests, or deletes code is refused, and so is one whose test files would\nshare a name, because hidden tests are flattened into one folder. As a check, a fix from\nthis project's own history (<code>8b1b0e7</code>, with <code>--runner pytest --build \"pip install .\"</code>)\nimports into a task that validates.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Replay and fork</h2><a id=\"user-content-replay-and-fork\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Replay and fork\" href=\"#replay-and-fork\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>agentoscopy replay &lt;trial_id&gt;</code> reruns a recorded trial in a fresh sandbox with the same\ntask version, agent config, and seed. Each model call is answered with the response\nrecorded at the same step, at no cost, as long as the agent sends the same request it sent\nthen; tool calls run live. A different request, or a call the original never made, stops\nthe replay with <code>REPLAY_DIVERGED</code> at that step. The command exits <code>0</code> when the replay ends\nwith the original outcome after the same model calls, and <code>1</code> otherwise. A replay is its\nown one-trial run; its trial page links to the original and to a side-by-side view.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>agentoscopy fork &lt;trial_id&gt; --at-step N</code> answers the model calls before step N from the\nrecording, whatever the agent asks, and makes step N and later live. Add <code>--agent CONFIG</code>\nto continue with another config, or <code>--inject TEXT</code> to add a message to the request at\nstep N, and see what would have happened. A recorded answer that calls a tool the new\nconfig lacks stops the fork with <code>REPLAY_DIVERGED</code>. Replayed answers reach the agent\nwithout their thinking blocks: the provider binds those to the conversation that produced\nthem and rejects them in the fork's later live calls. Its trial page links to the original\nand to the side-by-side view.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code>agentoscopy bisect &lt;trial_id&gt; --agent CONFIG</code> finds the step where a failed trial went\nwrong. It forks the trial with a config that can pass the task, the rescue config: forking\nat step k keeps the trial's own first k - 1 model answers and lets the rescue config take\nover from step k. While those forks still pass, the trial's mistake has not happened yet;\nonce they fail, it has. A binary search finds the last step from which the trial can be\nrescued, so the answer recorded at that step is the one that sealed the failure, and the\ncommand prints a side-by-side link to see what the rescue config did instead.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Live calls vary, so each step runs <code>--trials</code> forks (3 by default) and counts as rescued\nwhen most of them pass. Both ends are checked first: if the rescue config fails the task\nfrom step 1, or still passes with every recorded answer kept, no step is blamed and the\ncommand exits <code>1</code>. <code>--budget-usd</code> (2 by default) caps live model spend across all forks.\nEach fork reserves the task's per-trial cap before it starts, as trials in a run do, so a\nbudget below that cap is refused with <code>BUDGET_BELOW_TRIAL_CAP</code>. Each fork run is labelled\n<code>bisect</code> and shows up in the run list. The search assumes that a trial that cannot be\nrescued from one step cannot be rescued from later steps either, so every probe is printed\nwith its pass count.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For example, one of the failed Haiku trials in the screenshot above (<code>add-deep-merge</code>, nine\nmodel calls) was bisected with <code>configs/claude-sonnet.yaml</code> as the rescue config:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"  fork at step 1: 3 of 3 passed, rescued\n  fork at step 2: 3 of 3 passed, rescued\n  fork at step 3: 0 of 3 passed, not rescued\n  fork at step 5: 0 of 3 passed, not rescued\n  fork at step 10: 0 of 3 passed, not rescued\nstep 2: the trial can still be rescued by taking over at step 2, but not once its own\nrecorded answer at step 2 is kept. That answer sealed the failure.\"><pre lang=\"text\" class=\"notranslate\"><code>  fork at step 1: 3 of 3 passed, rescued\n  fork at step 2: 3 of 3 passed, rescued\n  fork at step 3: 0 of 3 passed, not rescued\n  fork at step 5: 0 of 3 passed, not rescued\n  fork at step 10: 0 of 3 passed, not rescued\nstep 2: the trial can still be rescued by taking over at step 2, but not once its own\nrecorded answer at step 2 is kept. That answer sealed the failure.\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Haiku's answer at step 2 read the protected test file. Once that was kept, Sonnet too\nappended its own tests to the file in every fork and was vetoed; taking over one step\nearlier, it passed every time. The 15 forks cost $0.24.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Tests</h2><a id=\"user-content-tests\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Tests\" href=\"#tests\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"uv run pytest                    # integration tests are skipped if Docker is not running\nuv run pytest tests/chaos        # kills a run mid-flight and resumes it\nuv run pytest -m &quot;not integration&quot;\nuv run ruff check . &amp;&amp; uv run ruff format --check agentoscopy tests\"><pre>uv run pytest                    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> integration tests are skipped if Docker is not running</span>\nuv run pytest tests/chaos        <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> kills a run mid-flight and resumes it</span>\nuv run pytest -m <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>not integration<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>\nuv run ruff check <span class=\"pl-c1\">.</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">&amp;&amp;</span> uv run ruff format --check agentoscopy tests</pre></div>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">License</h2><a id=\"user-content-license\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: License\" href=\"#license\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">MIT License; see <a href=\"LICENSE\">LICENSE</a>.</p>\n</article></div>";
